# Battlefront with two opponents: the hasty token attacks Bot2 while Memnite attacks Bot3, so X is 2 and two cards leave
# Bot1's library together while both opponents' libraries stay untouched. "You may play those cards" both ways: the Plains
# is played from exile on Bot1's next turn, the Ornithopter is left, and after that turn ends the permission is gone.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mountain
Memnite
Black Lotus
Mox Pearl
Mox Jet
Worf, Defiant Commander
Island
Island
Island
Plains
Ornithopter
Island x9

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Bot3 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mountain.Play
Bot1.Hand.Memnite.Cast
[T4 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Red)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Worf, Defiant Commander.Cast
? Bot1.Mana =
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot3.Pass
? Exile.Count = 0
Bot1.Attack(Klingon Warrior Token > Bot2; Memnite > Bot3)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot3.Pass
? Exile.Count = 2
? Bot1.Library.Count = 9
? Exile = Ornithopter; Plains
? Bot2.Library.Count = 12
? Bot3.Library.Count = 12
[T7 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Exile.Plains.Play
? Exile = Ornithopter
[T10 Bot1.Main1]
! Bot1.Exile.Ornithopter.Cast

[Expect]
Turn = 10
Bot1.Battlefield.Plains.Tapped = false
Exile = Ornithopter
